<!--
  COLLECTION track row, trailing action glyph.

  Frozen canonical: `Track Item N` > `Container` > `Button` > `Container` >
  `arrow_forward`, light node 2409:31572, dark 2444:18186. The instance is
  Material's `arrow_forward` at 24x24 and carries **rotation: 45** - the only
  rotation on either canonical page, and confirmed on all three track items. Its
  wrapper is 33.94 square, which is 24 * sqrt(2), the bounding box of a 24 square
  turned through 45 degrees; that is the arithmetic that makes the rotation a
  measurement rather than a reading of the preview.

  So the arrow points north-east, not east. Figma's rotation is positive
  counter-clockwise and Android's is positive clockwise, hence -45 here for the
  same glyph direction.

  Unlike the empty-state illustration and the header overflow dots, this one is
  not authored from its box: `arrow_forward` is a named Material instance, so the
  Material path is the path, exactly as docs/COLLECTION-3.6.6.md took Material's
  `favorite` for the empty-state heart.

  Tint comes from the view; the fill here is only what an untinted preview shows.
-->
